  - For each split point i (1 <= i < len): integer part `d[0..i)`, fractional part `d[i..len)`. Valid if:
    - Integer part doesn't have leading zeros (unless it's exactly "0", i.e., i == 1 and d[0] == '0').
    - Fractional part doesn't end with '0' (trailing zeros in fraction are not allowed since "1.0" is invalid).

