This is a simple problem. For a string to be alternating, it must either start with '0' (pattern "0101...") or start with '1' (pattern "1010...").

Count the number of changes needed for each pattern, return the minimum.

For pattern starting with '0': at index i, expected char is '0' if i is even, '1' if i is odd.
For pattern starting with '1': at index i, expected char is '1' if i is even, '0' if i is odd.

Count mismatches for pattern 0. Mismatches for pattern 1 = n - mismatches for pattern 0 (since every position mismatches exactly one of the two patterns).

Return min(count0, n - count0).

