Since all fees are positive, any walk containing a cycle is dominated by the walk with the cycle removed (less time, less cost), so considering all walks via this DP yields the same optimum as considering simple paths. Reads at time `t` only come from row `t - w < t` (as `w ≥ 1`), so processing times in increasing order is safe.

Complexity: `O(maxTime · m)` time (~10⁶ operations), `O(maxTime · n)` memory (~8 MB with a flat `Float64Array`). Sorting edges by time with an activation pointer skips edges whose weight exceeds the current time.

