This is a simple problem. For each rectangle, the largest square it can form has side min(l, w). Find the max of these mins, then count how many rectangles have min equal to max.

Let me write the TypeScript solution:

```typescript
function countGoodRectangles(rectangles: number[][]): number {
    let maxLen = 0;
    let count = 0;
    for (const [l, w] of rectangles) {
        const side = Math.min(l, w);
        if (side > maxLen) {
            maxLen = side;
            count = 1;
        } else if (side === maxLen) {
            count++;
        }
    }
    return count;
}
```

This is a single pass solution. Time O(n), space O(1).

